Article 14 Where a mining right holder requests the infringer to compensate for the following losses caused by cross-border prospecting or mining, the People's Court shall uphold such request:
(1) the value of mineral products obtained by the infringer through cross-border prospecting or mining;
(2) the value of mineral products that the mining right holder could have extracted in accordance with the approved preliminary mine design, safety facility design or mining plan but was unable to extract due to the infringement;
(3) the increased mining costs and mine ecological restoration expenses incurred by the mining right holder due to the infringement.
Where the mining right holder requests that the value of mineral products specified in the preceding paragraph be calculated based on the market price at the time the loss occurred, the People's Court shall uphold such request.
Where a prospecting right holder requests the infringer to compensate for increased prospecting costs, restoration expenses and losses of benefits obtainable according to law caused by cross-border prospecting or mining, the People's Court shall uphold such request.

Article 15 In any of the following circumstances, the People's Court may determine that it constitutes "placing a burden on mineral resources" as provided in Article 32 of the Mineral Resources Law:
(1) the land area occupied by the construction project overlaps with the legally registered prospecting or mining area, or although there is no overlap, prospecting or mining is prohibited within a certain range around the construction project in accordance with relevant regulations, directly affecting the exercise of mineral rights;
(2) prospecting or mining is restricted within a certain range around the construction project, and according to relevant regulations, the mineral rights holder needs to obtain the consent of the construction project right holder or the approval of the relevant administrative authority before prospecting or mining, but fails to obtain such consent or approval within a reasonable period.
